{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1486006-opinions-on-guide-to-the-night","id":1486006,"title":"Opinions on guide to the night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-07T13:15:18-07:00","id":1486006,"title":"Opinions on guide to the night","content":"So what the title says","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T14:16:23-07:00","id":1486363,"title":"","content":"It was ok. I see <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/257465/Guide-to-the-Night?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Night</a></b> as an additional chapter to the VtR 2 ed. rulebook (similar to the VtR 1 ed. Storytelling and Antagonists chapter). It provided me with some good ideas on how to see the presence of clans and covenants in the 2 ed. version. Now, is it an essential book? For newcomers it might be a very good addition, and provide some out of the box thinking. For veterans to VtR? Perhaps less so, as some areas are re-tread from the first edition books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-24-2023, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T16:27:52-07:00","id":1486371,"title":"","content":"Like Cabaal said, it is great for new storytellers since it gives a lot of suggestions on how to build elements for your chronicle (most of the CoD line is really lacking in this aspect) and the alternate setting are interesting but if you already are familiar with requiem and already have a few 1st ed supplements then it's nothing special, not horrible by any means but not something I would deem essential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T01:19:36-07:00","id":1486394,"title":"","content":"An example; Guide to the NIght has a pretty good chapter on coteries. If you've only read the VtR 2 ed. rulebook, this will be of help to the reader. If you have already read the book <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1441/Coteries?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Coteries</a></b> for the first edition, much less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-24-2023, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}